{"resourceIdentifier":"5078","resourceName":"CTR Metropolitana Landfill Gas","description":"The proposed project activity has the objective to capture, flare and generate electricity through the use of landfill gas (LFG)  produced in anaerobic conditions into the landfill called “CTR Metropolitana Landfill” (hereinafter referred to as “CTR Metropolitana Landfill”) located in the city of Pilar in the state of Alagoas, Brazil. The landfill started the operation on May 2015, receiving solid waste (type Class II-A Inert and Class II-B Non-inert) .\r\nThe project activity results in greenhouse gas (GHG) emission reduction from the CTR Metropolitana landfill through two ways:\r\n\r\ni.\tBurning CH4 in flares and/or group generators;\r\nii.     The amount of electricity generated in the project activity is dispatched to the Brazilian Interconnected Electrical System (SIN), avoiding the dispatch of an equal amount of energy produced by fossil-fuelled thermal plants to that grid. The initiative avoids CO2 emissions and contributes to the regional and national sustainable development.\r\n\r\nThe project activity aims to capture and to flare the LFG and to generate electricity through the implementation of a power generation plant using LFG. The generation installed capacity during the first crediting period will be equal to 3.71 MW.\r\n\r\nThe project constructed an efficient capture, collection and flaring system to burn CH4 (a greenhouse gas), and this reduced odours and adverse environmental impacts. Moreover, it installs generators that combusts the LFG to produce electricity, using part of the electricity for self-consumption and the other part is exported to the grid. The flares are kept in operation due to LFG excess, periods when electricity is not be produced or other operational considerations. The LFG power plant has 3.71 MW installed capacity.","location":{"latitude":-9.661166,"longitude":-36.650243},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2024-07-05","endExclusive":"2024-08-05","endInclusive":"2024-08-04"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"5078"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Alagoas"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ALAGOAS AMBIENTAL S/A"},{"type":"string","value":"Alagoas, Brazil"},{"type":"string","value":"+5511971998933"},{"type":"string","value":"fernando.freitas@veolia.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Verification approval requested"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"93308"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Waste handling and disposal"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ACM0001"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"0 Hectares"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Earthood Services Limited"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"14/04/2025"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 10/08/2022 - 09/08/2029"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=112226&IDKEY=m8723kjnf7kjandsaslmdv09887vaksmrmnwqkjoiuanfnfuq0a154759654","documentType":"Draft Project Description","documentName":"VCS_PD_DRAFT_5078_24APR2024.pdf","uploadDate":"2024-05-02T20:17:22.533Z"},{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=115433&IDKEY=a903q4jsafkasjfu90amnmasdfkaidflnmdf9348r09dmfasdf4159182107","documentType":"Draft Project Description","documentName":"VCS_PD_PCP_5078_05JUL2024.pdf","uploadDate":"2024-07-05T19:46:27.327Z"},{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?F